    "Question #: 1": {
      "Title": "Exam ASVAB Test topic 1 question 8 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A printing plant that produces baseball cards has a monthly overhead of $6,000. It costs 18 cents to print each card, and the cards sell for 30 cents each."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "How many cards must the printing plant sell each month in order to make a profit?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. 30,000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. 40,000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. 50,000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. 60,000"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: C \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Let x = the number of cards printed and sold each month. Therefore, cost is equal to 6000 + 18x, and revenue is equal to 0.30x. You're looking for the point where revenue is greater than the cost (revenue > cost). The inequity is 0.30x > 6000 + 18x. Subtracting 18x from both sides of the inequity results in 0.12x > 6000."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Divide both sides by 0.12. The result is that x > 50,000. The printing plant would have to print and sell 50,000 cards per month to make a profit."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Let x = the number of cards printed and sold each month. Therefore, cost is equal to 6000 + 18x, and revenue is equal to 0.30x. You're looking for the point where revenue is greater than the cost (revenue > cost). The inequity is 0.30x > 6000 + 18x. Subtracting 18x from both sides of the inequity results in 0.12x > 6000."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Divide both sides by 0.12. The result is that x > 50,000. The printing plant would have to print and sell 50,000 cards per month to make a profit."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Vote_count": []
