    "Question #: 4": {
      "Title": "Exam ASVAB Test topic 1 question 72 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A painter has painted a picture on a piece of canvas that measures 10 \u05b3\u2014 14 inches. In order to accommodate a frame, he has left an unpainted margin of 1 inch all the way around."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "What part of the canvas has been painted?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. 80%"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. 75%"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. 25%"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. 66%"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: A \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The area of the entire piece of canvas = 10 inches \u05b3\u2014 14 inches = 140 square inches. The portion painted on equals 8 inches \u05b3\u2014 12 inches = 112 square inches."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "(This is determined by subtracting 1 inch from the length of each side to account for the margin.) The portion used for painting can be expressed as a fraction: 112\u05d2\u201e"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "140. Reduce this fraction (divide 112 by 140) to determine that 80% of the canvas is covered with paint."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The area of the entire piece of canvas = 10 inches \u05b3\u2014 14 inches = 140 square inches. The portion painted on equals 8 inches \u05b3\u2014 12 inches = 112 square inches."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "(This is determined by subtracting 1 inch from the length of each side to account for the margin.) The portion used for painting can be expressed as a fraction: 112\u05d2\u201e"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "140. Reduce this fraction (divide 112 by 140) to determine that 80% of the canvas is covered with paint."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Vote_count": [
        {
          "voted_answers": "A",
          "vote_count": 1,
          "is_most_voted": true
        }
      ]
    },
